.TH WINDOWBORDER-DAEMON 1 "2026-10-05" "kwin-windowborder 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
windowborder-daemon \- D-Bus backend for the Window Border KWin script extension
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B windowborder-daemon
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serves the \f(CWorg.kde.windowborder\fR name on the session bus and runs
\fBwindowborder-native\fR(1) on request. The KWin script extension can only
\f(CWreadConfig\fR and \f(CWcallDBus\fR \- it cannot write files or start
processes \- while giving a window a border means writing
\f(CWkwinrulesrc\fR and \f(CWbreezerc\fR. This daemon is that missing half:
.IP \(bu 2
a click in the window menu calls \f(CWAddApp\fR or \f(CWRemoveApp\fR;
.IP \(bu 2
the daemon polls \f(CW~/.config/kwinrc\fR every two seconds. Saving the
settings panel of the extension only writes the application list there, and
neither KWin nor the already running script reacts to that, so the daemon
triggers the sync itself.
.PP
It is started on demand through D-Bus activation
(\fI/usr/share/dbus-1/services/org.kde.windowborder.service\fR) and at login
through \fI/etc/xdg/autostart/windowborder-daemon.desktop\fR. Running it by
hand is only useful for debugging.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --backend \fIpath\fR
Path to \fBwindowborder-native\fR(1). By default it is looked up next to this
script, then in \f(CW$PATH\fR.
.TP
.B --python \fIinterpreter\fR
Interpreter used to run the backend (default: the one running the daemon).
.TP
.B --no-watch
Do not poll \f(CWkwinrc\fR; only serve the D-Bus interface.
.TP
.B --verbose
Log every request to standard error.
.SH D-BUS INTERFACE
.TP
.B Name
\f(CWorg.kde.windowborder\fR
.TP
.B Object path
\f(CW/WindowBorder\fR
.TP
.B Interface
\f(CWorg.kde.windowborder\fR
.SH METHODS
.TP
.B AddApp(s app) -> b
Add an application to the list and apply.
.TP
.B RemoveApp(s app) -> b
Remove an application from the list and apply.
.TP
.B Sync() -> b
Apply the application list as it currently is in \f(CWkwinrc\fR.
.TP
.B Reapply() -> b
Regenerate the rules from the current list and apply them.
.TP
.B GetApps() -> as
The current application list.
.TP
.B Version() -> s
Daemon version.
.TP
.B Quit() -> b
Stop the daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR windowborder-native (1)
